<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-constant">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`AGENT_AUTOPILOT: number = 8192`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`integer AGENT_AUTOPILOT = 8192;`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>The integer constant AGENT_AUTOPILOT has the value 0x2000</p>
  <p>This value is set when the user selects "Go Here" on the ground, or uses the optional Double-Click Auto-Pilot feature.</p>
  <p>Under Viewer 2.0 and later, it is also set when:</p>
</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Member Of</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>AgentInfo</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>

      <div class="label-stack">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <ul>
    <li>the user selects "Sit Here" on the ground.</li>
    <li>an object is selected or edited, <i>and</i> that selection can trigger a <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Control" target="_blank">control</a> (<a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/CONTROL_ROT_RIGHT" target="_blank">CONTROL_ROT_RIGHT</a> and <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/CONTROL_ROT_LEFT" target="_blank">CONTROL_ROT_LEFT</a> can be activated when selecting an object near the far right or left edge of the screen).</li>
  </ul>
